## Issue Description
#4775 was supposed to fix the format of transactions' JSON representation so that, among other things, server-added fields like `date` and `ledger_index` were _not_ included at the same level as canonical fields like `Account` and `DeliverMax` that are part of the signed transaction object.

In API v2, `date` and `ledger_index` are still included in the `tx_json` nested object. Per the comments in PR #4775:

> @Bronek wrote:
> no, want to keep it where it is (in addition to the new location) in API version 2; then remove in API version 3

However, even in API version 3 the fields are still there. (Also, I personally disagree with leaving them there in the first place—the point of the API versioning is to make breaking changes like this.)

## Steps to Reproduce
Query a transaction using the `tx` method and `"api_version": 3`.

Example `tx` WebSocket request [[link]](https://xrpl.org/resources/dev-tools/websocket-api-tool?server=wss%3A%2F%2Fs.devnet.rippletest.net%3A51233%2F&req=%7B%20%20%22command%22%3A%20%22tx%22%2C%0A%20%20%22transaction%22%3A%20%224483695FD3502B0536B4F1311E39F656442212A85EDDC72E6037253376CCDD33%22%2C%0A%20%20%22binary%22%3A%20false%2C%0A%20%20%22api_version%22%3A%203%0A%7D):

```json
{
  "command": "tx",
  "transaction": "4483695FD3502B0536B4F1311E39F656442212A85EDDC72E6037253376CCDD33",
  "binary": false,
  "api_version": 3
}
```

## Expected Result

The `result.tx_json` field should contain only the canonical fields of the transaction, while the other lower-case fields (like `hash`, `ledger_index`, `close_time_iso`, etc.) are at the `result` level.

## Actual Result
The `tx_json` nested object contains a `date` field (which should not exist) and a `ledger_index` field (which is a duplicate of the one at the higher level).

